{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 161, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "tc_dot: a block FMA of 4 f16 products and an f32 c (Ampere's f16 HMMA with f32 accumulate, as modelled by arXiv 2512.07004)\n  semantics: products exact; aligned to E, the largest exponent among the products and c (at least -132), in a window of 24 fractional bits, each term truncated toward zero; one exact integer sum; normalised once and truncated to f32\n  bound (derived): |tc_dot - sum T| < 5 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S| <= 5 2^-24 max|T| + 2^-23 |sum T| + ..., T the 5 products and c, S the window's sum\n    each term loses less than one unit of the window, 2^(E-24), by its truncation (none for a term on the window's grid); the final truncation to 24 bits loses less than 2^-23 |S|; and 2^E <= max|T| where the largest term's significand is at least 1 (normal inputs)\n    relative to the largest term, not to sum |T|: with cancellation the result's own relative error is unbounded\n  checked on 3 random blocks (sampled, seed 1): the operation as written and an independent transcription agree on 3; the bound holds on 3, the error at most 0.285 of it\n  largest error relative to max|T|: 8.84e-08 (2^-24 = 5.96e-08); relative to |sum T|: 8.8e-08\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 161, "ok": true, "cmd": "tcdot", "ucas": "tcdot n 4 samples 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tcdot", "terms": 5, "bound": "(n+1) 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S|", "max_error_over_max_term": 8.84331531085374e-08, "max_error_over_sum": 8.797505229623997e-08}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sampled", "points": 3, "max_diff": 0.2850227838440354, "passed": true, "text": "the bound on random blocks, and the operation against an independent transcription"}], "files": [], "text": "tc_dot: a block FMA of 4 f16 products and an f32 c (Ampere's f16 HMMA with f32 accumulate, as modelled by arXiv 2512.07004)\n  semantics: products exact; aligned to E, the largest exponent among the products and c (at least -132), in a window of 24 fractional bits, each term truncated toward zero; one exact integer sum; normalised once and truncated to f32\n  bound (derived): |tc_dot - sum T| < 5 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S| <= 5 2^-24 max|T| + 2^-23 |sum T| + ..., T the 5 products and c, S the window's sum\n    each term loses less than one unit of the window, 2^(E-24), by its truncation (none for a term on the window's grid); the final truncation to 24 bits loses less than 2^-23 |S|; and 2^E <= max|T| where the largest term's significand is at least 1 (normal inputs)\n    relative to the largest term, not to sum |T|: with cancellation the result's own relative error is unbounded\n  checked on 3 random blocks (sampled, seed 1): the operation as written and an independent transcription agree on 3; the bound holds on 3, the error at most 0.285 of it\n  largest error relative to max|T|: 8.84e-08 (2^-24 = 5.96e-08); relative to |sum T|: 8.8e-08\n"}, "isError": false}}
